IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: Part 7, ss 210 to 212 (and the repealed ss 211A to 211J, 213, 214).
-- Compromise or arrangement with creditors, members and holders of units of shares (s 210); the information the notice of
-- the meeting must carry (s 211); the Court's approval of a reconstruction or amalgamation scheme (s 212).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Nothing here takes a person's point of view; the seat layer (sgd-seat.l4) does.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29 and the Guide's rulings; see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sgd)").
--   JUST TRUE   the section's own test is met on the facts given.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no to this case in its own words (a "means" definition, a condition introduced by "if", "unless",
--               "until"; a list closed with "only"; a flat negative; a period or "where" condition the text states).
--   NOTHING     not covered: the text lists without closing the list, says "includes", is silent, points to a power or
--               instrument outside the sources, or limits a grant in its own wording and the case falls outside the limit.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every branch that answers no carries `-- FALSE-kind (...)`; every branch that answers "not covered" carries `-- NOTHING-kind (...)`.
-- Periods are counted only by sg-periods.l4 (conventions P1 to P9 of the keel: assumed, not ruled by a lawyer).
-- The Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 is not a source: what it decides is an input, named for the fact.
-- Money is a NUMBER in Singapore dollars. A date is written Date day month year.

§ `One record shape for the penalties of ss 210 to 215J`

-- What a penalty provision of this Part states: the highest fine, the longest imprisonment and whether the text allows both.
-- Used for ss 210(9), 211(5), 212(3), 215I(6) and 215J(5). The shape is declared once, here, under its first provision.
DECLARE `s 210(9) penalty` HAS
    `s 210(9) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 210(9) the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `s 210(9) the text allows both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 210(9) the person is also liable to a default penalty` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Part 7: arrangements, reconstructions and amalgamations (heading only)`

-- Lines 20183 to 20187 are the Part heading ("PART 7 ARRANGEMENTS, RECONSTRUCTIONS AND AMALGAMATIONS"): not operative, no rule.

§ `Section 210(1) and (2): the Court may order a meeting; who may apply`

-- The three compromises s 210(1)(a), (b) and (c) name, and the case outside them.
DECLARE `s 210(1) proposal` IS ONE OF
    `s 210(1)(a) a compromise or an arrangement between a company and its creditors or any class of them`
    `s 210(1)(b) a compromise or an arrangement between a company and its members or any class of them`
    `s 210(1)(c) a compromise or an arrangement between a company and holders of units of shares of the company or any class of them`
    `s 210(1) a proposal of some other kind`

-- The applicants s 210(2) names, and anyone else.
DECLARE `s 210(2) applicant` IS ONE OF
    `s 210(2)(a) the liquidator of the company`
    `s 210(2)(b)(i) the company`
    `s 210(2)(b)(ii) a creditor of the company`
    `s 210(2)(b)(ii) a member of the company`
    `s 210(2)(b)(ii) a holder of units of shares of the company`
    `s 210(2) some other person`

-- (2): "The persons referred to in subsection (1) are": (a) for a company being wound up, the liquidator; (b) in any other case, the company
-- or any creditor, member or holder of units of shares. A list the text states as a definition ("are"): read as closed (fork F-210-1).
-- src:20209 | (2) The persons referred to in subsection (1) are —
-- src:20211 | (a) in the case of a company being wound up — the liquidator;
-- src:20212 | and
-- src:20214 | (b) in any other case —
-- src:20216 | (i) the company; or
-- src:20218 | (ii) any creditor, member or holder of units of shares of
-- src:20219 | the company.
@ref s 210(2) (src:20209-20219)
GIVEN `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      applicant IS A `s 210(2) applicant`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(2) the person is a person referred to in subsection (1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER applicant
    WHEN `s 210(2)(a) the liquidator of the company` THEN
        IF `the company is being wound up`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in any other case — (i) the company; or (ii) any creditor, member or holder of units of shares of the company" (the liquidator is the applicant only "in the case of a company being wound up")
    WHEN `s 210(2)(b)(i) the company` THEN
        IF `the company is being wound up`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) in the case of a company being wound up — the liquidator" (for a company being wound up the persons are the liquidator; the company is listed only "in any other case")
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 210(2)(b)(ii) a creditor of the company` THEN
        IF `the company is being wound up`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) in the case of a company being wound up — the liquidator" (creditors are listed only "in any other case")
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 210(2)(b)(ii) a member of the company` THEN
        IF `the company is being wound up`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) in the case of a company being wound up — the liquidator" (members are listed only "in any other case")
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 210(2)(b)(ii) a holder of units of shares of the company` THEN
        IF `the company is being wound up`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) in the case of a company being wound up — the liquidator" (holders of units of shares are listed only "in any other case")
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The persons referred to in subsection (1) are —" (a list stated as a definition; fork F-210-1)

-- (1): "Where a compromise or an arrangement is proposed between (a) a company and its creditors ...; (b) ... its members ...; or (c) ... holders
-- of units of shares ..., the Court may, on the application in a summary way of any person referred to in subsection (2), order a meeting ... to be summoned".
-- A power ("may"), gated by "Where" and by "on the application ... of any person referred to in subsection (2)": a "may" gated by "where" and
-- "on application" (split site (ii); the periods ruling (b) answers JUST FALSE; fork F-210-2 and the count in NOTES.md).
-- src:20191 | 210.—(1) Where a compromise or an arrangement is proposed
-- src:20192 | between —
-- src:20194 | (a) a company and its creditors or any class of them;
-- src:20196 | (b) a company and its members or any class of them; or
-- src:20198 | (c) a company and holders of units of shares of the company or
-- src:20199 | any class of them,
-- src:20201 | the Court may, on the application in a summary way of any person
-- src:20202 | referred to in subsection (2), order a meeting of the creditors, the
-- src:20203 | members of the company, the holders of units of shares of the
-- src:20204 | company, or a class of such persons, to be summoned in such manner
-- src:20205 | as the Court directs.
@ref s 210(1) (src:20191-20205)
GIVEN proposal IS A `s 210(1) proposal`
      `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      applicant IS A `s 210(2) applicant`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(1) the Court may order a meeting to be summoned` MEANS
    CONSIDER proposal
    WHEN `s 210(1) a proposal of some other kind` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a compromise or an arrangement is proposed between — (a) a company and its creditors or any class of them; (b) a company and its members or any class of them; or (c) a company and holders of units of shares of the company or any class of them" (a "where" condition, periods ruling (b); fork F-210-2)
    OTHERWISE
        IF `s 210(2) the person is a person referred to in subsection (1)` `the company is being wound up` applicant EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on the application in a summary way of any person referred to in subsection (2)" (an application gate; fork F-210-2)

§ `Section 210(3): adjourning the meeting`

-- The vote at the meeting, as a witness could state it. "Value" is the value of the creditors' claims, or of the members' or holders' shares or
-- units: the text does not say how the value of a member's interest is measured, so the figure is supplied (fork F-210-3).
DECLARE `s 210(3) vote` HAS
    `s 210(3) the number of persons present and voting in person or by proxy` IS A NUMBER
    `s 210(3) the number of those persons who voted in favour` IS A NUMBER
    `s 210(3) the value held by the persons present and voting` IS A NUMBER
    `s 210(3) the value held by those who voted in favour` IS A NUMBER

-- "a majority in number": more than half of the persons present and voting (assumed: a majority is more than half).
GIVEN vote IS A `s 210(3) vote`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 210(3) a majority in number of those present and voting voted in favour` MEANS
    ((vote's `s 210(3) the number of those persons who voted in favour`) TIMES 2) GREATER THAN (vote's `s 210(3) the number of persons present and voting in person or by proxy`)

-- "representing three-fourths in value": at least three-fourths of the value held by those present and voting (assumed: "three-fourths" is a floor, fork F-210-4).
GIVEN vote IS A `s 210(3) vote`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 210(3) those who voted in favour represent three-fourths in value of those present and voting` MEANS
        ((vote's `s 210(3) the value held by those who voted in favour`) TIMES 4) AT LEAST ((vote's `s 210(3) the value held by the persons present and voting`) TIMES 3)
    AND (vote's `s 210(3) the value held by the persons present and voting`) GREATER THAN 0

-- (3): "A meeting held pursuant to an order made under subsection (1) may be adjourned from time to time if the resolution for the adjournment is
-- approved by a majority in number representing three-fourths in value of ... present and voting either in person or by proxy at the meeting."
-- A power ("may be adjourned") whose "if" gate failed answers NOTHING (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-210-5).
-- src:20223 | (3) A meeting held pursuant to an order made under subsection (1)
-- src:20224 | may be adjourned from time to time if the resolution for the
-- src:20225 | adjournment is approved by a majority in number representing
-- src:20226 | three‑fourths in value of —
-- src:20228 | (a) the creditors or class of creditors;
-- src:20230 | (b) the members or class of members; or
-- src:20235 | (c) the holders of units of shares or class of holders of units of
-- src:20236 | shares,
-- src:20238 | present and voting either in person or by proxy at the meeting.
@ref s 210(3) (src:20223-20238)
GIVEN vote IS A `s 210(3) vote`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(3) the meeting may be adjourned` MEANS
    IF    `s 210(3) a majority in number of those present and voting voted in favour` vote
      AND `s 210(3) those who voted in favour represent three-fourths in value of those present and voting` vote
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be adjourned from time to time if the resolution for the adjournment is approved by a majority in number representing three-fourths in value" (a grant whose "if" gate failed; grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1)

§ `Section 210(3AA) and (3AB): when the compromise or arrangement binds`

-- The party the compromise or arrangement may bind, as (3AA) lists them (the rendering interleaves the labels of the two limbs: finding 1 in NOTES.md).
DECLARE `s 210(3AA) party` IS ONE OF
    `s 210(3AA)(a) the liquidator of a company in the course of being wound up`
    `s 210(3AA)(a) a contributory of a company in the course of being wound up`
    `s 210(3AA)(b) the company, where it is not in the course of being wound up`
    `s 210(3AA) a creditor of the class concerned`
    `s 210(3AA) a member of the class concerned`
    `s 210(3AA) a holder of units of shares of the class concerned`
    `s 210(3AA) some other person`

-- (3AB): the three conditions. (a) unless the Court orders otherwise, a majority in number agrees; (b) the majority in number, or such number as the Court
-- may order, represents three-fourths in value; (c) the compromise or arrangement is approved by order of the Court.
-- "Unless the Court orders otherwise" once met: the number the Court orders replaces the majority in number in (a) and (b) (fork F-210-6).
-- src:20272 | (3AB) The conditions referred to in subsection (3AA) are as
-- src:20273 | follows:
-- src:20275 | (a) unless the Court orders otherwise, a majority in number
-- src:20276 | of —
-- src:20278 | (i) the creditors or class of creditors;
-- src:20280 | (ii) the members or class of members; or
-- src:20282 | (iii) the holders of units of shares or class of holders of
-- src:20283 | units of shares,
-- src:20288 | (a) present and voting either in person or by proxy at the
-- src:20289 | meeting or the adjourned meeting agrees to the
-- src:20290 | compromise or arrangement;
-- src:20292 | (b) the majority in number referred to, or such number as the
-- src:20293 | Court may order, under paragraph (a) represents
-- src:20294 | three‑fourths in value of —
-- src:20296 | (i) the creditors or class of creditors;
-- src:20298 | (ii) the members or class of members; or
-- src:20300 | (iii) the holders of units of shares or class of holders of
-- src:20301 | units of shares,
-- src:20303 | (b) present and voting either in person or by proxy at the
-- src:20304 | meeting or the adjourned meeting, as the case may be;
-- src:20306 | (c) the compromise or arrangement is approved by order of the
-- src:20307 | Court.
@ref s 210(3AB) (src:20272-20307)
GIVEN vote IS A `s 210(3) vote`
      `the Court has ordered that a number other than a majority in number must agree` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of persons the Court has ordered must agree` IS A NUMBER
      `the compromise or arrangement is approved by order of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(3AB) the conditions for the compromise or arrangement to be binding are satisfied` MEANS
    IF    (IF `the Court has ordered that a number other than a majority in number must agree`
           THEN (vote's `s 210(3) the number of those persons who voted in favour`) AT LEAST `the number of persons the Court has ordered must agree`
           ELSE `s 210(3) a majority in number of those present and voting voted in favour` vote)
      AND `s 210(3) those who voted in favour represent three-fourths in value of those present and voting` vote
      AND `the compromise or arrangement is approved by order of the Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions referred to in subsection (3AA) are as follows" (the conditions are listed as a definition; a condition not met is a condition not satisfied)

-- (3AA): "If the conditions set out in subsection (3AB) are satisfied, a compromise or an arrangement is binding" (a) for a company in the course of being
-- wound up, on the liquidator and contributories and on all the creditors, members or holders of units of shares of the class, as the case may be; (b) for
-- any other company, on the company and on all of them.
-- src:20242 | (3AA) If the conditions set out in subsection (3AB) are satisfied, a
-- src:20243 | compromise or an arrangement is binding —
-- src:20245 | (a) in the case of a company in the course of being wound up,
-- src:20246 | on the liquidator and contributories of the company, and on
-- src:20247 | all —
-- src:20249 | (i) the creditors or class of creditors;
-- src:20251 | (ii) the members or class of members; or
-- src:20253 | (iii) the holders of units of shares or class of holders of
-- src:20254 | units of shares,
-- src:20256 | (a) as the case may be; or
-- src:20258 | (b) in the case of any other company, on the company and on
-- src:20259 | all —
-- src:20261 | (i) the creditors or class of creditors;
-- src:20263 | (ii) the members or class of members; or
-- src:20265 | (iii) the holders of units of shares or class of holders of
-- src:20266 | units of shares,
-- src:20268 | (b) as the case may be.
@ref s 210(3AA) (src:20242-20268)
GIVEN `the conditions set out in subsection (3AB) are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is in the course of being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      party IS A `s 210(3AA) party`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(3AA) the compromise or arrangement is binding on the party` MEANS
    IF NOT `the conditions set out in subsection (3AB) are satisfied`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the conditions set out in subsection (3AB) are satisfied, a compromise or an arrangement is binding" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))
    ELSE CONSIDER party
         WHEN `s 210(3AA)(a) the liquidator of a company in the course of being wound up` THEN
             IF `the company is in the course of being wound up` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) in the case of a company in the course of being wound up, on the liquidator and contributories"
         WHEN `s 210(3AA)(a) a contributory of a company in the course of being wound up` THEN
             IF `the company is in the course of being wound up` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) in the case of a company in the course of being wound up, on the liquidator and contributories of the company"
         WHEN `s 210(3AA)(b) the company, where it is not in the course of being wound up` THEN
             IF `the company is in the course of being wound up` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) in the case of any other company, on the company and on all —"
         WHEN `s 210(3AA) a creditor of the class concerned` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 210(3AA) a member of the class concerned` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 210(3AA) a holder of units of shares of the class concerned` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names the liquidator, contributories, the company and the creditors, members or holders of units of the class, and says nothing of any other person

§ `Sections 210(3A), (4) and (4A): the Court's approval`

-- (3A) and (4A) are shown "[Deleted by Act 40 of 2018]": no rule (coverage rows "repealed or blank in this text").
-- (4): "The Court may grant its approval to a compromise or arrangement subject to such alterations or conditions as it thinks just." The judgment is the
-- Court's: it is a conditional input ("if the Court thinks it just"). A grant limited by its own wording and the case outside it: NOTHING (fork F-210-7).
-- src:20313 | (4) The Court may grant its approval to a compromise or
-- src:20314 | arrangement subject to such alterations or conditions as it thinks just.
@ref s 210(4) (src:20313-20314)
GIVEN `the Court thinks the alteration or condition just` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(4) the Court may grant its approval subject to the alteration or condition` MEANS
    IF `the Court thinks the alteration or condition just`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to such alterations or conditions as it thinks just" (a grant limited by the Court's own judgment; the case outside it is not covered, grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-210-7)

§ `Section 210(5): when the order takes effect`

-- (5): "An order under subsection (3AB)(c) has no effect until a copy of the order is lodged with the Registrar": a bar (ruling (d) of 2026-11-05):
-- JUST TRUE before the copy is lodged ("cannot yet have effect"), JUST FALSE after. The function never says the order has taken effect.
-- src:20320 | (5) An order under subsection (3AB)(c) has no effect until a copy of
-- src:20321 | the order is lodged with the Registrar, and upon being so lodged, the
-- src:20322 | order takes effect on and from the date of lodgment or such earlier
-- src:20323 | date as the Court may determine and as may be specified in the order.
@ref s 210(5) (src:20320-20323)
GIVEN `a copy of the order has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(5) the order cannot yet have effect` MEANS
    IF `a copy of the order has been lodged with the Registrar`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has no effect until a copy of the order is lodged with the Registrar" (an "until" bar: once the copy is lodged the bar is lifted; ruling (d) of 2026-11-05)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (5): "upon being so lodged, the order takes effect on and from the date of lodgment or such earlier date as the Court may determine and as may be
-- specified in the order." Not lodged: no date yet. An "earlier date" not earlier than the lodgment is not "such earlier date": not covered (fork F-210-8).
@ref s 210(5) (src:20320-20323)
GIVEN `a copy of the order has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE
      `the order specifies a date that the Court has determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date specified in the order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 210(5) the date from which the order takes effect` MEANS
    IF NOT `a copy of the order has been lodged with the Registrar`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection gives the order no date until a copy is lodged
    ELSE IF `the order specifies a date that the Court has determined`
         THEN (IF `the date specified in the order` LESS THAN `the date the copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar`
               THEN JUST `the date specified in the order`
               ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on and from the date of lodgment or such earlier date as the Court may determine and as may be specified in the order" (a date that is not earlier than the date of lodgment is not "such earlier date"; fork F-210-8)
         ELSE JUST `the date the copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar`

§ `Sections 210(6) and (7): the order annexed to the constitution`

-- (6): "Subject to subsection (7), a copy of every order made under subsection (3AB)(c) must be annexed to every copy of the constitution of the company
-- issued after the order has been made." (7): the Court may exempt the company or determine the period during which it must comply.
-- A copy issued before the order is outside the duty's own scope: NOTHING (scope limit, periods ruling (c); fork F-210-9).
-- src:20327 | (6) Subject to subsection (7), a copy of every order made under
-- src:20328 | subsection (3AB)(c) must be annexed to every copy of the
-- src:20329 | constitution of the company issued after the order has been made.
-- src:20333 | (7) The Court may, by order, exempt a company from compliance
-- src:20334 | with the requirements of subsection (6) or determine the period
-- src:20335 | during which the company must so comply.
@ref s 210(6) (src:20327-20335)
GIVEN `the copy of the constitution is issued after the order has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has by order exempted the company from compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has determined the period during which the company must comply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy of the constitution is issued within that period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(6) a copy of the order must be annexed to the copy of the constitution` MEANS
    IF NOT `the copy of the constitution is issued after the order has been made`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to every copy of the constitution of the company issued after the order has been made" (a copy issued before the order is outside the scope; periods ruling (c); fork F-210-9)
    ELSE IF `the Court has by order exempted the company from compliance`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (7)" and "The Court may, by order, exempt a company from compliance with the requirements of subsection (6)" (the exemption lifts the duty)
         ELSE IF `the Court has determined the period during which the company must comply` AND (NOT `the copy of the constitution is issued within that period`)
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or determine the period during which the company must so comply" (a period the Court fixed; a copy issued outside it is outside the duty)
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (7): the Court's power: it "may, by order, exempt a company from compliance with the requirements of subsection (6) or determine the period".
DECLARE `s 210(7) what the Court does` IS ONE OF
    `s 210(7) exempts the company from compliance with subsection (6)`
    `s 210(7) determines the period during which the company must comply with subsection (6)`
    `s 210(7) does something else`

-- src:20333 | (7) The Court may, by order, exempt a company from compliance
-- src:20334 | with the requirements of subsection (6) or determine the period
-- src:20335 | during which the company must so comply.
@ref s 210(7) (src:20333-20335)
GIVEN `what the Court does` IS A `s 210(7) what the Court does`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(7) the Court may do it by order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what the Court does`
    WHEN `s 210(7) exempts the company from compliance with subsection (6)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 210(7) determines the period during which the company must comply with subsection (6)` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, by order, exempt a company from compliance with the requirements of subsection (6) or determine the period during which the company must so comply" (a grant naming two things and nothing else; fork F-210-12)

§ `Section 210(8): the accountants' or solicitors' report`

-- (8): "Where any such compromise or arrangement ... has been proposed, the directors of the company must (a) if a meeting of the members of the company by
-- resolution so directs, instruct such accountants or solicitors or both as are named in the resolution to report on the proposals and forward their report or
-- reports to the directors as soon as possible; and (b) make such report or reports available at the registered office of the company for inspection by the
-- shareholders, creditors and holders of units of shares of the company at least 7 days before the date of any meeting ordered by the Court to be summoned".
-- src:20337 | (8) Where any such compromise or arrangement (whether or not for
-- src:20338 | the purposes of or in connection with a scheme for the reconstruction
-- src:20343 | of any company or companies or the amalgamation of any 2 or more
-- src:20344 | companies) has been proposed, the directors of the company must —
-- src:20346 | (a) if a meeting of the members of the company by resolution
-- src:20347 | so directs, instruct such accountants or solicitors or both as
-- src:20348 | are named in the resolution to report on the proposals and
-- src:20349 | forward their report or reports to the directors as soon as
-- src:20350 | possible; and
@ref s 210(8)(a) (src:20337-20350)
GIVEN `a compromise or arrangement has been proposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a meeting of the members of the company has by resolution directed that accountants or solicitors or both report on the proposals` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(8)(a) the directors must instruct the accountants or solicitors named in the resolution to report` MEANS
    IF `a compromise or arrangement has been proposed` AND `a meeting of the members of the company has by resolution directed that accountants or solicitors or both report on the proposals`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any such compromise or arrangement ... has been proposed, the directors of the company must — (a) if a meeting of the members of the company by resolution so directs" (a "where" and an "if" condition on a duty; periods ruling (b), marginal reading (a))

-- (8)(b): at least 7 days before the date of the meeting the Court ordered: "not less than N days before X" (P5): the last day is the meeting day minus 7.
-- src:20352 | (b) make such report or reports available at the registered
-- src:20353 | office of the company for inspection by the shareholders,
-- src:20354 | creditors and holders of units of shares of the company at
-- src:20355 | least 7 days before the date of any meeting ordered by the
-- src:20356 | Court to be summoned as provided in subsection (1).
@ref s 210(8)(b) (src:20352-20356)
GIVEN `the day of the meeting ordered by the Court` IS A DATE
      `the day the reports were made available at the registered office` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(8)(b) the reports have been made available at least 7 days before the meeting` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is at least a period before` `the day the reports were made available at the registered office` `the day of the meeting ordered by the Court` 7 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "make such report or reports available at the registered office of the company for inspection ... at least 7 days before the date of any meeting" (a duty with a stated period, not met; the provision's own question)

-- The last day for the reports to be available, as a number of days after a start day (for the trace of the regulative rule below).
GIVEN `the day of the meeting ordered by the Court` IS A DATE
      `the start day of the trace` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 210(8)(b) the number of days from the start day to the latest day for the reports` MEANS
    (`period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the day of the meeting ordered by the Court` 7 Days) MINUS `the start day of the trace`

§ `Section 210(9): the offence`

-- (9): "Every company which makes default in complying with subsection (6) or (8) and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an
-- offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $2,000."
-- An unmet element of the offence (no default): the provision's own question, JUST FALSE (split site (i); Guide line 98; fork F-210-10).
-- src:20360 | (9) Every company which makes default in complying with
-- src:20361 | subsection (6) or (8) and every officer of the company who is in
-- src:20362 | default shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- src:20363 | to a fine not exceeding $2,000.
@ref s 210(9) (src:20360-20363)
GIVEN `the company has made default in complying with subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has made default in complying with subsection (8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(9) the company is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the company has made default in complying with subsection (6)` OR `the company has made default in complying with subsection (8)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork F-210-10): "Every company which makes default in complying with subsection (6) or (8) ... shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the company guilty of nothing on these facts

@ref s 210(9) (src:20360-20363)
GIVEN `the company has made default in complying with subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has made default in complying with subsection (8)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
      position IS A `s 4(1) "officer" what the person is`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(9) the officer is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company has made default in complying with subsection (6)` OR `the company has made default in complying with subsection (8)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork F-210-10): "Every company which makes default ... and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- the company's default is an element of the officer's
    ELSE IF NOT `the officer is in default`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork F-210-10): "every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- the officer is not in default
         ELSE `s 4(1) "officer" the person is an officer of the corporation` position

@ref s 210(9) (src:20360-20363)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 210(9) penalty`
`s 210(9) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates`
    THEN JUST (`s 210(9) penalty` OF 2000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty; "a fine not exceeding $2,000" and no imprisonment

§ `Section 210(10): the Court may restrain proceedings against the company`

-- (10): "Where no order has been made or resolution passed for the winding up of a company and any such compromise or arrangement has been proposed between the
-- company and its creditors or any class of such creditors, the Court may ... on the application in a summary way of the company or of any member, creditor or holder
-- of units of shares of the company restrain further proceedings in any action or proceeding against the company except by permission of the Court".
-- A "may" gated by "Where" and "on the application": split site (ii), JUST FALSE by periods ruling (b), listed in the fork register (F-210-2).
-- src:20367 | (10) Where no order has been made or resolution passed for the
-- src:20368 | winding up of a company and any such compromise or arrangement
-- src:20369 | has been proposed between the company and its creditors or any class
-- src:20370 | of such creditors, the Court may, in addition to any of its powers, on
-- src:20371 | the application in a summary way of the company or of any member,
-- src:20372 | creditor or holder of units of shares of the company restrain further
-- src:20373 | proceedings in any action or proceeding against the company except
-- src:20374 | by permission of the Court and subject to such terms as the Court
-- src:20375 | imposes.
@ref s 210(10) (src:20367-20375)
GIVEN `no order has been made or resolution passed for the winding up of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a compromise or arrangement has been proposed between the company and its creditors or any class of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made in a summary way by the company or by a member, creditor or holder of units of shares of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(10) the Court may restrain further proceedings against the company` MEANS
    IF    `no order has been made or resolution passed for the winding up of the company`
      AND `a compromise or arrangement has been proposed between the company and its creditors or any class of them`
      AND `the application is made in a summary way by the company or by a member, creditor or holder of units of shares of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where no order has been made or resolution passed for the winding up of a company and any such compromise or arrangement has been proposed between the company and its creditors or any class of such creditors, the Court may" (a "where" gate on a power; periods ruling (b); fork F-210-2)

-- What the restraint means for a person with an action against the company: no further proceedings "except by permission of the Court and subject to such terms as the Court imposes".
@ref s 210(10) (src:20367-20375)
GIVEN `the Court has restrained further proceedings against the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has given permission to proceed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(10) further proceedings against the company may continue` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Court has restrained further proceedings against the company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says what follows an order restraining proceedings; without one it says nothing about them
    ELSE IF `the Court has given permission to proceed`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "restrain further proceedings in any action or proceeding against the company except by permission of the Court" (a flat bar with one exception)

§ `Sections 210(10A) and (10B): money held in trust for a person`

-- (10A): "Where the terms of any compromise or arrangement approved under this section provides for any money or other consideration to be held by or on behalf of any party
-- in trust for any person, the person holding the money or other consideration may, after the expiration of 2 years and must before the expiration of 10 years from the date
-- on which the money or other consideration was received by the person, transfer the money or other consideration to the Official Receiver."
-- "after the expiration of 2 years": the first day is the day after the last day of the 2-year period (P1, P4). "before the expiration of 10 years": up to and including the last
-- day of the 10-year period (the period expires at its end). A period the text fixes in its own words: outside it, JUST FALSE (periods ruling (a); fork F-210-11).
-- src:20381 | (10A) Where the terms of any compromise or arrangement
-- src:20382 | approved under this section provides for any money or other
-- src:20383 | consideration to be held by or on behalf of any party to the
-- src:20384 | compromise or arrangement in trust for any person, the person
-- src:20385 | holding the money or other consideration may, after the expiration of
-- src:20386 | 2 years and must before the expiration of 10 years from the date on
-- src:20391 | which the money or other consideration was received by the person,
-- src:20392 | transfer the money or other consideration to the Official Receiver.
@ref s 210(10A) (src:20381-20392)
GIVEN `the terms of the compromise or arrangement provide for money or other consideration to be held in trust for a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the money or other consideration was received by the person holding it` IS A DATE
      `the day of the transfer to the Official Receiver` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(10A) the transfer to the Official Receiver is within the time the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF NOT `the terms of the compromise or arrangement provide for money or other consideration to be held in trust for a person`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the terms of any compromise or arrangement approved under this section provides for any money or other consideration to be held ... in trust for any person" (a "where" condition; periods ruling (b))
    ELSE IF `the day of the transfer to the Official Receiver` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the money or other consideration was received by the person holding it` 2 Years)
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, after the expiration of 2 years" (a period the text fixes in its own words; a transfer on or before the last day of the 2 years is too early; periods ruling (a))
         ELSE IF `the day of the transfer to the Official Receiver` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the money or other consideration was received by the person holding it` 10 Years)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must before the expiration of 10 years from the date on which the money or other consideration was received" (a period the text fixes in its own words; a transfer after the last day of the 10 years is late; periods ruling (a))

-- The number of days from a start day to the last day of the 10 years (for the trace of the duty to transfer).
GIVEN `the day the money or other consideration was received by the person holding it` IS A DATE
      `the start day of the trace` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 210(10A) the number of days from the start day to the last day before the 10 years expire` MEANS
    (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the money or other consideration was received by the person holding it` 10 Years) MINUS `the start day of the trace`

-- (10B): "The Official Receiver must (a) deal with any moneys received under subsection (10A) as if the moneys were paid to the Official Receiver under section 197 of the
-- Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018; and (b) sell or dispose of any other consideration received under subsection (10A) in such manner as the Official Receiver thinks
-- fit and must deal with the proceeds of such sale or disposal as if it were moneys paid to the Official Receiver under section 197 of the ... Act 2018." What section 197 does is not a source.
DECLARE `s 210(10B) treatment` IS ONE OF
    `s 210(10B)(a) dealt with as if the moneys were paid to the Official Receiver under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    `s 210(10B)(b) sold or disposed of in the manner the Official Receiver thinks fit, the proceeds dealt with as if moneys paid under section 197 of that Act`

-- src:20396 | (10B) The Official Receiver must —
-- src:20398 | (a) deal with any moneys received under subsection (10A) as
-- src:20399 | if the moneys were paid to the Official Receiver under
-- src:20400 | section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:20401 | Dissolution Act 2018; and
-- src:20403 | (b) sell or dispose of any other consideration received under
-- src:20404 | subsection (10A) in such manner as the Official Receiver
-- src:20405 | thinks fit and must deal with the proceeds of such sale or
-- src:20406 | disposal as if it were moneys paid to the Official Receiver
-- src:20407 | under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:20408 | Dissolution Act 2018.
@ref s 210(10B) (src:20396-20408)
GIVEN `the thing received under subsection (10A) is money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing received under subsection (10A) is other consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 210(10B) treatment`
`s 210(10B) how the Official Receiver must deal with what is received` MEANS
    IF `the thing received under subsection (10A) is money`
    THEN JUST `s 210(10B)(a) dealt with as if the moneys were paid to the Official Receiver under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    ELSE IF `the thing received under subsection (10A) is other consideration`
         THEN JUST `s 210(10B)(b) sold or disposed of in the manner the Official Receiver thinks fit, the proceeds dealt with as if moneys paid under section 197 of that Act`
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) deal with any moneys received under subsection (10A) ...; and (b) sell or dispose of any other consideration received under subsection (10A)" (the subsection says what the Official Receiver does with money and with other consideration received under (10A), and nothing of anything else)

§ `Section 210(11): the words defined`

-- "arrangement" includes a reorganisation of the share capital of a company by the consolidation of shares of different classes or by the division of shares into shares of
-- different classes or by both these methods. An "includes" list is open: outside it, NOTHING.
-- src:20414 | “arrangement” includes a reorganisation of the share capital of a
-- src:20415 | company by the consolidation of shares of different classes or
-- src:20416 | by the division of shares into shares of different classes or by
-- src:20417 | both these methods;
@ref s 210(11) "arrangement" (src:20414-20417)
GIVEN `the thing is a reorganisation of the share capital of a company by the consolidation of shares of different classes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a reorganisation of the share capital of a company by the division of shares into shares of different classes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(11) "arrangement" the thing is within the word arrangement` MEANS
    IF    `the thing is a reorganisation of the share capital of a company by the consolidation of shares of different classes`
       OR `the thing is a reorganisation of the share capital of a company by the division of shares into shares of different classes`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“arrangement” includes a reorganisation of the share capital of a company by ..." leaves the list open

-- "company" means any corporation liable to be wound up under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 (whether it is liable is a supplied fact).
-- src:20419 | “company” means any corporation liable to be wound up under
-- src:20420 | the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018;
@ref s 210(11) "company" (src:20419-20420)
GIVEN `the corporation is liable to be wound up under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(11) "company" the body is a company` MEANS
    IF `the corporation is liable to be wound up under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“company” means any corporation liable to be wound up under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018" (a "means" definition)

-- "holder of units of shares" does not include a person who holds units of shares only beneficially.
-- src:20422 | “holder of units of shares” does not include a person who holds
-- src:20423 | units of shares only beneficially.
@ref s 210(11) "holder of units of shares" (src:20422-20423)
GIVEN `the person holds units of shares only beneficially` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(11) "holder of units of shares" the person is a holder of units of shares` MEANS
    IF `the person holds units of shares only beneficially`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“holder of units of shares” does not include a person who holds units of shares only beneficially" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the definition only excludes; it does not say who else is a holder

§ `Section 211: the information that must go with the notice of the meeting`

-- The two kinds of notice s 211(1) distinguishes.
DECLARE `s 211(1) notice` IS ONE OF
    `s 211(1)(a) a notice summoning the meeting sent to a creditor, member or holder of units of shares of the company`
    `s 211(1)(b) a notice summoning the meeting given by advertisement`

-- (1): "Where a meeting is summoned under section 210, there must (a) with every notice summoning the meeting which is sent to a creditor, member or holder of units of shares of the
-- company — be sent also a statement explaining the effect of the compromise or arrangement and in particular stating any material interests of the directors ...; and (b) in every
-- notice summoning the meeting which is given by advertisement — be included either such a statement or a notification of the place at which and the manner in which [persons] ... may obtain copies".
-- src:20430 | 211.—(1) Where a meeting is summoned under section 210, there
-- src:20431 | must —
-- src:20433 | (a) with every notice summoning the meeting which is sent to
-- src:20434 | a creditor, member or holder of units of shares of the
-- src:20435 | company — be sent also a statement explaining the effect
-- src:20436 | of the compromise or arrangement and in particular stating
-- src:20437 | any material interests of the directors, whether as directors
-- src:20442 | or as members, creditors or holders of units of shares of the
-- src:20443 | company or otherwise, and the effect thereon of the
-- src:20444 | compromise or arrangement in so far as it is different from
-- src:20445 | the effect on the like interests of other persons; and
-- src:20447 | (b) in every notice summoning the meeting which is given by
-- src:20448 | advertisement — be included either such a statement or a
-- src:20449 | notification of the place at which and the manner in which
-- src:20450 | creditors, members or holders of units of shares of the
-- src:20451 | company entitled to attend the meeting may obtain copies
-- src:20452 | of such a statement.
@ref s 211(1) (src:20430-20452)
GIVEN `a meeting is summoned under section 210` IS A BOOLEAN
      notice IS A `s 211(1) notice`
      `a statement explaining the effect of the compromise or arrangement is sent with the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement states any material interests of the directors and the effect on them so far as different from the effect on the like interests of other persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice includes such a statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice includes a notification of the place at which and the manner in which copies of such a statement may be obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 211(1) the notice carries what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `a meeting is summoned under section 210`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a meeting is summoned under section 210, there must" (a "where" condition on a duty; periods ruling (b), marginal reading (a))
    ELSE CONSIDER notice
         WHEN `s 211(1)(a) a notice summoning the meeting sent to a creditor, member or holder of units of shares of the company` THEN
             IF    `a statement explaining the effect of the compromise or arrangement is sent with the notice`
               AND `the statement states any material interests of the directors and the effect on them so far as different from the effect on the like interests of other persons`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) with every notice summoning the meeting which is sent to a creditor, member or holder of units of shares of the company — be sent also a statement explaining the effect ... and in particular stating any material interests of the directors" (a duty not met; the provision's own question)
         WHEN `s 211(1)(b) a notice summoning the meeting given by advertisement` THEN
             IF    `the notice includes such a statement`
                OR `the notice includes a notification of the place at which and the manner in which copies of such a statement may be obtained`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in every notice summoning the meeting which is given by advertisement — be included either such a statement or a notification of the place at which and the manner in which" (a duty not met; the provision's own question)

-- (2): "Where the compromise or arrangement affects the rights of debenture holders, the statement must give the like explanation with respect to the trustee for the debenture holders".
-- src:20456 | (2) Where the compromise or arrangement affects the rights of
-- src:20457 | debenture holders, the statement must give the like explanation with
-- src:20458 | respect to the trustee for the debenture holders as, under
-- src:20459 | subsection (1), a statement is required to give with respect to the
-- src:20460 | directors.
@ref s 211(2) (src:20456-20460)
GIVEN `the compromise or arrangement affects the rights of debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives the like explanation with respect to the trustee for the debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 211(2) the statement gives what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `the compromise or arrangement affects the rights of debenture holders`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the compromise or arrangement affects the rights of debenture holders, the statement must give the like explanation" (a "where" condition on a duty; periods ruling (b), marginal reading (a))
    ELSE IF `the statement gives the like explanation with respect to the trustee for the debenture holders`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the statement must give the like explanation with respect to the trustee for the debenture holders" (a duty not met; the provision's own question)

-- (3): "Where a notice given by advertisement includes a notification that copies of such a statement can be obtained, every creditor, member or holder of units of shares of the company
-- entitled to attend the meeting must on making application in the manner indicated by the notice be furnished by the company free of charge with a copy of the statement." (Hohfeld: the person's claim; the company's duty.)
-- src:20462 | (3) Where a notice given by advertisement includes a notification
-- src:20463 | that copies of such a statement can be obtained, every creditor,
-- src:20464 | member or holder of units of shares of the company entitled to attend
-- src:20465 | the meeting must on making application in the manner indicated by
-- src:20466 | the notice be furnished by the company free of charge with a copy of
-- src:20467 | the statement.
@ref s 211(3) (src:20462-20467)
GIVEN `the notice given by advertisement includes a notification that copies of the statement can be obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a creditor, member or holder of units of shares of the company entitled to attend the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has made application in the manner indicated by the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 211(3) the company must furnish the person with a copy of the statement free of charge` MEANS
    IF    `the notice given by advertisement includes a notification that copies of the statement can be obtained`
      AND `the person is a creditor, member or holder of units of shares of the company entitled to attend the meeting`
      AND `the person has made application in the manner indicated by the notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a notice given by advertisement includes a notification that copies of such a statement can be obtained, every creditor, member or holder of units of shares of the company entitled to attend the meeting must on making application in the manner indicated by the notice be furnished" (a "where" condition and a condition on the person; periods ruling (b), marginal reading (a))

-- (4): "Each director and each trustee for debenture holders must give notice to the company of such matters relating to the director or the trustee as may be necessary for the purposes
-- of this section within 7 days of the receipt of a request in writing for information as to such matters." "within 7 days of the receipt": an act on the day of receipt is in time ("not later than").
-- src:20471 | (4) Each director and each trustee for debenture holders must give
-- src:20472 | notice to the company of such matters relating to the director or the
-- src:20473 | trustee as may be necessary for the purposes of this section within
-- src:20474 | 7 days of the receipt of a request in writing for information as to such
-- src:20475 | matters.
@ref s 211(4) (src:20471-20475)
GIVEN `the day the request in writing for information was received` IS A DATE
      `the day the director or trustee gave notice to the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 211(4) the director or trustee gave notice within 7 days of the receipt of the request` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the request in writing for information was received` `the day the director or trustee gave notice to the company` 7 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must give notice to the company ... within 7 days of the receipt of a request in writing" (a duty with a stated period, not met; the provision's own question)

-- The last day for the notice (for the trace), as a number of days after the day the request was received.
GIVEN `the day the request in writing for information was received` IS A DATE
      `the start day of the trace` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 211(4) the number of days from the start day to the last day for the notice` MEANS
    (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the request in writing for information was received` 7 Days) MINUS `the start day of the trace`

-- (6): "For the purpose of subsection (5), the liquidator of the company and any trustee for debenture holders are deemed to be officers of the company."
-- src:20483 | (6) For the purpose of subsection (5), the liquidator of the company
-- src:20484 | and any trustee for debenture holders are deemed to be officers of the
-- src:20485 | company.
@ref s 211(6) (src:20483-20485)
GIVEN `the person is the liquidator of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a trustee for debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 211(6) the person is deemed to be an officer of the company for subsection (5)` MEANS
    IF `the person is the liquidator of the company` OR `the person is a trustee for debenture holders`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection deems two kinds of person to be officers; it says nothing of anyone else (s 4(1) "officer" answers for the rest)

-- (5): "Where default is made in complying with any requirement of this section, the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence and
-- shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months." The text says "or", not "or to both" (contrast s 7A(6)).
-- src:20477 | (5) Where default is made in complying with any requirement of
-- src:20478 | this section, the company and every officer of the company who is in
-- src:20479 | default shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- src:20480 | to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:20481 | exceeding 12 months.
@ref s 211(5) (src:20477-20481)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with a requirement of this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 211(5) the company is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with a requirement of this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork F-211-1): "Where default is made in complying with any requirement of this section, the company ... shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the company guilty of nothing on these facts

-- (5) with (6) and (7): an officer (or the liquidator, or a trustee for debenture holders, deemed officers by (6)) who is in default is guilty, unless the person shows (7) that the default
-- was due to another director's or trustee's refusal to supply the particulars.
@ref s 211(5) (src:20477-20481)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with a requirement of this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
      position IS A `s 4(1) "officer" what the person is`
      `the person is the liquidator of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a trustee for debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 211(5) the officer is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `default is made in complying with a requirement of this section`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork F-211-1): "Where default is made in complying with any requirement of this section, the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty" -- the company's default is an element of the officer's
    ELSE IF NOT `the officer is in default`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork F-211-1): "every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- the officer is not in default
         ELSE IF `s 211(6) the person is deemed to be an officer of the company for subsection (5)` `the person is the liquidator of the company` `the person is a trustee for debenture holders` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE `s 4(1) "officer" the person is an officer of the corporation` position

-- (7): "Despite subsection (5), a person shall not be liable under that subsection if the person shows that the default was due to the refusal of any other person, being a director or trustee
-- for debenture holders, to supply the necessary particulars as to the person's interests." A defence: when it is not shown, "this section gives no defence on these facts" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (b)).
-- src:20490 | (7) Despite subsection (5), a person shall not be liable under that
-- src:20491 | subsection if the person shows that the default was due to the refusal
-- src:20492 | of any other person, being a director or trustee for debenture holders,
-- src:20493 | to supply the necessary particulars as to the person’s interests.
@ref s 211(7) (src:20490-20493)
GIVEN `the person shows that the default was due to the refusal of another director or trustee for debenture holders to supply the necessary particulars as to the person's interests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 211(7) the section gives the person a defence` MEANS
    IF `the person shows that the default was due to the refusal of another director or trustee for debenture holders to supply the necessary particulars as to the person's interests`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person shall not be liable under that subsection if the person shows that the default was due to the refusal of any other person" (a defence not shown: this section gives no defence on these facts, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b); it does not say the person is liable)

-- (5) and (7) together: the person is liable under subsection (5) unless the (7) defence is shown.
@ref s 211(7) (src:20490-20493)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of the offence under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person shows that the default was due to the refusal of another director or trustee for debenture holders to supply the necessary particulars as to the person's interests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 211(5) and (7) the person is liable under subsection (5)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is guilty of the offence under subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork F-211-1): the person is not made guilty by subsection (5) on these facts
    ELSE IF `s 211(7) the section gives the person a defence` `the person shows that the default was due to the refusal of another director or trustee for debenture holders to supply the necessary particulars as to the person's interests` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Despite subsection (5), a person shall not be liable under that subsection if the person shows that the default was due to the refusal of any other person"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:20477 | (5) Where default is made in complying with any requirement of
-- src:20478 | this section, the company and every officer of the company who is in
-- src:20479 | default shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- src:20480 | to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:20481 | exceeding 12 months.
@ref s 211(5) (src:20477-20481)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 210(9) penalty`
`s 211(5) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates`
    THEN JUST (`s 210(9) penalty` OF 5000, 12, FALSE, FALSE)   -- "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months": "or", not "or to both"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- 211A to 211J: "[Repealed by Act 40 of 2018]" (coverage row; no rule).

§ `Section 212: the Court's order approving a reconstruction or an amalgamation scheme`

-- The matters s 212(1)(a) to (f) lets the order provide for, and any other.
DECLARE `s 212(1) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 212(1)(a) the transfer to the transferee company of the whole or any part of the undertaking and of the property or liabilities of the transferor company`
    `s 212(1)(b) the allotting or appropriation by the transferee company of shares, debentures, policies or other like interests`
    `s 212(1)(c) the continuation by or against the transferee company of legal proceedings pending by or against the transferor company`
    `s 212(1)(d) the dissolution, without winding up, of the transferor company`
    `s 212(1)(e) the provision to be made for any persons who dissent from the compromise or arrangement`
    `s 212(1)(f) such incidental, consequential and supplemental matters as are necessary to secure that the reconstruction or amalgamation is fully and effectively carried out`
    `s 212(1) some other matter`

-- (1): "Where an application is made to the Court under this Part or section 71 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 for the approval of a compromise or arrangement and it is shown to the
-- Court that the compromise or arrangement has been proposed for the purposes of or in connection with a scheme for the reconstruction of any company or companies or the amalgamation of any 2 or more companies,
-- and that under the scheme the whole or any part of the undertaking or the property of any company concerned in the scheme ... is to be transferred to another company ..., the Court may either by the order
-- approving the compromise or arrangement or by any subsequent order provide for all or any of the following matters". A "may" gated by "Where": split site (ii), JUST FALSE by periods ruling (b) (F-212-1).
-- src:20499 | 212.—(1) Where an application is made to the Court under this Part
-- src:20500 | or section 71 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution
-- src:20501 | Act 2018 for the approval of a compromise or arrangement and it is
-- src:20502 | shown to the Court that the compromise or arrangement has been
-- src:20503 | proposed for the purposes of or in connection with a scheme for the
-- src:20504 | reconstruction of any company or companies or the amalgamation of
-- src:20505 | any 2 or more companies, and that under the scheme the whole or any
-- src:20506 | part of the undertaking or the property of any company concerned in
-- src:20507 | the scheme (called in this section the transferor company) is to be
-- src:20508 | transferred to another company (called in this section the transferee
-- src:20509 | company), the Court may either by the order approving the
-- src:20510 | compromise or arrangement or by any subsequent order provide
-- src:20511 | for all or any of the following matters:
-- src:20513 | (a) the transfer to the transferee company of the whole or any
-- src:20514 | part of the undertaking and of the property or liabilities of
-- src:20515 | the transferor company;
-- src:20517 | (b) the allotting or appropriation by the transferee company of
-- src:20518 | any shares, debentures, policies or other like interests in
-- src:20519 | that company which under the compromise or arrangement
-- src:20520 | are to be allotted or appropriated by that company to or for
-- src:20521 | any person;
-- src:20523 | (c) the continuation by or against the transferee company of
-- src:20524 | any legal proceedings pending by or against the transferor
-- src:20525 | company;
-- src:20527 | (d) the dissolution, without winding up, of the transferor
-- src:20528 | company;
-- src:20533 | (e) the provision to be made for any persons who, within such
-- src:20534 | time and in such manner as the Court directs, dissent from
-- src:20535 | the compromise or arrangement;
-- src:20537 | (f) such incidental, consequential and supplemental matters as
-- src:20538 | are necessary to secure that the reconstruction or
-- src:20539 | amalgamation is fully and effectively carried out.
@ref s 212(1) (src:20499-20539)
GIVEN `an application is made to the Court under Part 7 or section 71 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 for the approval of a compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is shown to the Court that the compromise or arrangement has been proposed for the purposes of or in connection with a scheme for the reconstruction of any company or companies or the amalgamation of any 2 or more companies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is shown to the Court that under the scheme the whole or any part of the undertaking or the property of a company concerned is to be transferred to another company` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 212(1) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 212(1) the Court may provide for the matter by its order` MEANS
    IF    `an application is made to the Court under Part 7 or section 71 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 for the approval of a compromise or arrangement`
      AND `it is shown to the Court that the compromise or arrangement has been proposed for the purposes of or in connection with a scheme for the reconstruction of any company or companies or the amalgamation of any 2 or more companies`
      AND `it is shown to the Court that under the scheme the whole or any part of the undertaking or the property of a company concerned is to be transferred to another company`
    THEN (CONSIDER matter
          WHEN `s 212(1) some other matter` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "provide for all or any of the following matters: (a) ...; (f) ..." (a grant over a listed set of matters; the text does not say the Court may provide for nothing else)
          OTHERWISE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an application is made to the Court under this Part or section 71 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 ... and it is shown to the Court that ... and that under the scheme" (a "where" gate on a power; periods ruling (b); fork F-212-1)

-- (1A): "[Deleted by Act 40 of 2018]" (coverage row; no rule).
-- (2): "Where an order made under this section provides for the transfer of property or liabilities, then by virtue of the order that property is transferred to and vests in, and those liabilities are
-- transferred to and become the liabilities of, the transferee company, free in the case of any particular property if the order so directs, from any charge which is by virtue of the compromise or
-- arrangement to cease to have effect."
-- src:20545 | (2) Where an order made under this section provides for the transfer
-- src:20546 | of property or liabilities, then by virtue of the order that property is
-- src:20547 | transferred to and vests in, and those liabilities are transferred to and
-- src:20548 | become the liabilities of, the transferee company, free in the case of
-- src:20549 | any particular property if the order so directs, from any charge which
-- src:20550 | is by virtue of the compromise or arrangement to cease to have effect.
@ref s 212(2) (src:20545-20550)
GIVEN `an order made under this section provides for the transfer of property or liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 212(2) the property vests in the transferee company and the liabilities become its liabilities by virtue of the order` MEANS
    IF `an order made under this section provides for the transfer of property or liabilities`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an order made under this section provides for the transfer of property or liabilities, then by virtue of the order that property is transferred" (a "where" condition on a deeming; periods ruling (b), marginal reading (a))

@ref s 212(2) (src:20545-20550)
GIVEN `the order directs that the particular property is free from the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge is by virtue of the compromise or arrangement to cease to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 212(2) the particular property vests free from the charge` MEANS
    IF `the order directs that the particular property is free from the charge` AND `the charge is by virtue of the compromise or arrangement to cease to have effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "free in the case of any particular property if the order so directs, from any charge which is by virtue of the compromise or arrangement to cease to have effect" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

-- (3): "Where an order is made under this section, every company in relation to which the order is made must lodge within 7 days of the making of the order (a) a copy of the order with the Registrar;
-- and (b) where the order relates to land, an office copy of the order with the appropriate authority ..., and every company which makes default in complying with this section and every officer of
-- the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $2,000 and also to a default penalty."
-- "within 7 days of the making of the order": an act on the day of the order is in time ("not later than"). A lodgment not yet made is not in time (the day is not a fact yet).
-- src:20552 | (3) Where an order is made under this section, every company in
-- src:20553 | relation to which the order is made must lodge within 7 days of the
-- src:20554 | making of the order —
-- src:20556 | (a) a copy of the order with the Registrar; and
-- src:20558 | (b) where the order relates to land, an office copy of the order
-- src:20559 | with the appropriate authority concerned with the
-- src:20560 | registration or recording of dealings in that land,
-- src:20562 | and every company which makes default in complying with this
-- src:20563 | section and every officer of the company who is in default shall be
-- src:20564 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:20565 | exceeding $2,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 212(3) (src:20552-20565)
GIVEN `the day the order was made` IS A DATE
      `the day of the lodgment, if it was made` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 212(3) the lodgment was made within 7 days of the making of the order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day of the lodgment, if it was made`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST d THEN `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the order was made` d 7 Days

@ref s 212(3) (src:20552-20565)
GIVEN `the day the order was made` IS A DATE
      `the day a copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the order relates to land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day an office copy of the order was lodged with the appropriate authority, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 212(3) the company has lodged what the subsection requires within 7 days of the making of the order` MEANS
    IF    `s 212(3) the lodgment was made within 7 days of the making of the order` `the day the order was made` `the day a copy of the order was lodged with the Registrar, if it was`
      AND (    (NOT `the order relates to land`)
            OR `s 212(3) the lodgment was made within 7 days of the making of the order` `the day the order was made` `the day an office copy of the order was lodged with the appropriate authority, if it was`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every company in relation to which the order is made must lodge within 7 days of the making of the order — (a) a copy of the order with the Registrar; and (b) where the order relates to land, an office copy" (a duty with a stated period, not met; the provision's own question)

-- The last day for lodging (for the trace), as a number of days after a start day.
GIVEN `the day the order was made` IS A DATE
      `the start day of the trace` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 212(3) the number of days from the start day to the last day for lodging` MEANS
    (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the order was made` 7 Days) MINUS `the start day of the trace`

@ref s 212(3) (src:20552-20565)
GIVEN `the company has made default in complying with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 212(3) the company is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the company has made default in complying with this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork F-212-2): "every company which makes default in complying with this section ... shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the company guilty of nothing on these facts

@ref s 212(3) (src:20552-20565)
GIVEN `the company has made default in complying with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
      position IS A `s 4(1) "officer" what the person is`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 212(3) the officer is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company has made default in complying with this section`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork F-212-2): "every company which makes default in complying with this section and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty" -- the company's default is an element of the officer's
    ELSE IF NOT `the officer is in default`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork F-212-2): "every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- the officer is not in default
         ELSE `s 4(1) "officer" the person is an officer of the corporation` position

@ref s 212(3) (src:20552-20565)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 210(9) penalty`
`s 212(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates`
    THEN JUST (`s 210(9) penalty` OF 2000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- "a fine not exceeding $2,000 and also to a default penalty" (the amount of the default penalty is s 408, not read)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- (4): "No vesting order, referred to in this section, has any effect or operation in transferring or otherwise vesting land until the appropriate entries are made with respect to the vesting of
-- that land by the appropriate authority." A bar (ruling (d) of 2026-11-05): JUST TRUE before the entries are made, JUST FALSE after.
-- src:20567 | (4) No vesting order, referred to in this section, has any effect or
-- src:20568 | operation in transferring or otherwise vesting land until the
-- src:20569 | appropriate entries are made with respect to the vesting of that land
-- src:20570 | by the appropriate authority.
@ref s 212(4) (src:20567-20570)
GIVEN `the appropriate entries have been made by the appropriate authority with respect to the vesting of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 212(4) the vesting order cannot yet have effect in vesting the land` MEANS
    IF `the appropriate entries have been made by the appropriate authority with respect to the vesting of the land`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has any effect or operation in transferring or otherwise vesting land until the appropriate entries are made" (an "until" bar: once the entries are made the bar is lifted; ruling (d) of 2026-11-05)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (5): "In this section — “liabilities” includes duties; “property” includes property, rights and powers of every description." Open lists: outside them, NOTHING.
-- src:20574 | “liabilities” includes duties;
@ref s 212(5) "liabilities" (src:20574-20574)
GIVEN `the thing is a duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 212(5) "liabilities" the thing is within the word liabilities` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a duty`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“liabilities” includes duties" leaves the list open

-- src:20576 | “property” includes property, rights and powers of every
-- src:20577 | description.
@ref s 212(5) "property" (src:20576-20577)
GIVEN `the thing is property, a right or a power of any description` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 212(5) "property" the thing is within the word property` MEANS
    IF `the thing is property, a right or a power of any description`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“property” includes property, rights and powers of every description" leaves the list open

-- (6): "In this section, “company” means any corporation liable to be wound up under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018."
-- src:20582 | (6) In this section, “company” means any corporation liable to be
-- src:20583 | wound up under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution
-- src:20584 | Act 2018.
@ref s 212(6) (src:20582-20584)
GIVEN `the corporation is liable to be wound up under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 212(6) "company" the body is a company` MEANS
    IF `the corporation is liable to be wound up under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section, “company” means any corporation liable to be wound up under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018" (a "means" definition)

-- ss 213 and 214: "[Repealed by S 675/2001]" (coverage rows; no rule).

§ `Regulative rules: the duties of ss 210 to 212 that name a party and an act`

-- The acts the duties below are about.
DECLARE `s 210 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 210(6) annex a copy of the order to a copy of the constitution`
    `s 210(8)(a) instruct the accountants or solicitors named in the resolution to report on the proposals`
    `s 210(8)(b) make the reports available at the registered office for inspection`
    `s 210(10A) transfer the money or other consideration to the Official Receiver`
    `s 211(3) furnish the person with a copy of the statement free of charge`
    `s 211(4) give notice to the company of the matters relating to the director or trustee`
    `s 212(3)(a) lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar`
    `s 212(3)(b) lodge an office copy of the order with the appropriate authority`

-- The Official Receiver is an office of the State and is not a constructor of the core's `Party` (NEEDS-CORE.md): a party of this module's own.
DECLARE `s 210(10B) party` IS ONE OF
    `s 210(10B) the Official Receiver`

DECLARE `s 210(10B) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 210(10B)(a) deal with the moneys received under subsection (10A) as if they were paid under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    `s 210(10B)(b) sell or dispose of the other consideration and deal with the proceeds as if they were moneys paid under section 197 of that Act`

-- (6): the company must annex. No time limit and no consequence of its own: a late act still reads FULFILLED; no trace reaches BREACH (NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path (sgd)").
-- src:20327 | (6) Subject to subsection (7), a copy of every order made under
-- src:20328 | subsection (3AB)(c) must be annexed to every copy of the
-- src:20329 | constitution of the company issued after the order has been made.
@ref s 210(6) (src:20327-20329)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 210 act`
`s 210(6) the company must annex a copy of the order to every copy of the constitution issued after the order` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 210(6) annex a copy of the order to a copy of the constitution`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "a copy of the order was not annexed to a copy of the constitution issued after the order was made"

-- (8)(a): the directors must instruct. "as soon as possible" is not a time limit the text fixes: no breach path.
-- src:20346 | (a) if a meeting of the members of the company by resolution
-- src:20347 | so directs, instruct such accountants or solicitors or both as
-- src:20348 | are named in the resolution to report on the proposals and
-- src:20349 | forward their report or reports to the directors as soon as
-- src:20350 | possible; and
@ref s 210(8)(a) (src:20346-20350)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 210 act`
`s 210(8)(a) a director must instruct the accountants or solicitors named in the resolution to report` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 210(8)(a) instruct the accountants or solicitors named in the resolution to report on the proposals`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the accountants or solicitors named in the resolution were not instructed to report"

-- (8)(b): at least 7 days before the date of the meeting. The deadline is a number of days from the start of the trace (see the helper above); a day later is a breach.
-- src:20352 | (b) make such report or reports available at the registered
-- src:20353 | office of the company for inspection by the shareholders,
-- src:20354 | creditors and holders of units of shares of the company at
-- src:20355 | least 7 days before the date of any meeting ordered by the
-- src:20356 | Court to be summoned as provided in subsection (1).
@ref s 210(8)(b) (src:20352-20356)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
      `the number of days from the start of the trace to the latest day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 210 act`
`s 210(8)(b) a director must make the reports available at the registered office at least 7 days before the meeting` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 210(8)(b) make the reports available at the registered office for inspection`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the start of the trace to the latest day`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the reports were not made available at the registered office at least 7 days before the date of the meeting"

-- (10A): the holder must transfer before the expiration of 10 years. The duty has a deadline (the last day of the 10 years), so a trace can reach BREACH.
-- src:20381 | (10A) Where the terms of any compromise or arrangement
-- src:20382 | approved under this section provides for any money or other
-- src:20383 | consideration to be held by or on behalf of any party to the
-- src:20384 | compromise or arrangement in trust for any person, the person
-- src:20385 | holding the money or other consideration may, after the expiration of
-- src:20386 | 2 years and must before the expiration of 10 years from the date on
-- src:20391 | which the money or other consideration was received by the person,
-- src:20392 | transfer the money or other consideration to the Official Receiver.
@ref s 210(10A) (src:20381-20392)
GIVEN who IS A Party
      `the number of days from the start of the trace to the last day before the 10 years expire` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 210 act`
`s 210(10A) the holder must transfer the money or other consideration to the Official Receiver before the 10 years expire` MEANS
    PARTY who
    MUST `s 210(10A) transfer the money or other consideration to the Official Receiver`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the start of the trace to the last day before the 10 years expire`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY who BECAUSE "the money or other consideration was not transferred to the Official Receiver before the expiration of 10 years from the date it was received"

-- (10B): the Official Receiver must deal with the moneys, and sell or dispose of other consideration. No time limit: no breach path.
-- src:20396 | (10B) The Official Receiver must —
-- src:20398 | (a) deal with any moneys received under subsection (10A) as
-- src:20399 | if the moneys were paid to the Official Receiver under
-- src:20400 | section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:20401 | Dissolution Act 2018; and
-- src:20403 | (b) sell or dispose of any other consideration received under
-- src:20404 | subsection (10A) in such manner as the Official Receiver
-- src:20405 | thinks fit and must deal with the proceeds of such sale or
-- src:20406 | disposal as if it were moneys paid to the Official Receiver
-- src:20407 | under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:20408 | Dissolution Act 2018.
@ref s 210(10B) (src:20396-20408)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 210(10B) party` `s 210(10B) act`
`s 210(10B)(a) the Official Receiver must deal with the moneys as if they were paid under section 197` MEANS
    PARTY `s 210(10B) the Official Receiver`
    MUST `s 210(10B)(a) deal with the moneys received under subsection (10A) as if they were paid under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 210(10B) the Official Receiver` BECAUSE "the moneys received under subsection (10A) were not dealt with as if paid under section 197"

@ref s 210(10B) (src:20403-20408)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 210(10B) party` `s 210(10B) act`
`s 210(10B)(b) the Official Receiver must sell or dispose of the other consideration` MEANS
    PARTY `s 210(10B) the Official Receiver`
    MUST `s 210(10B)(b) sell or dispose of the other consideration and deal with the proceeds as if they were moneys paid under section 197 of that Act`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 210(10B) the Official Receiver` BECAUSE "the other consideration received under subsection (10A) was not sold or disposed of, or its proceeds were not dealt with as moneys paid under section 197"

-- s 211(3): the company must furnish a copy free of charge. No time limit: no breach path.
-- src:20462 | (3) Where a notice given by advertisement includes a notification
-- src:20463 | that copies of such a statement can be obtained, every creditor,
-- src:20464 | member or holder of units of shares of the company entitled to attend
-- src:20465 | the meeting must on making application in the manner indicated by
-- src:20466 | the notice be furnished by the company free of charge with a copy of
-- src:20467 | the statement.
@ref s 211(3) (src:20462-20467)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 210 act`
`s 211(3) the company must furnish the person with a copy of the statement free of charge` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 211(3) furnish the person with a copy of the statement free of charge`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the person was not furnished with a copy of the statement free of charge"

-- s 211(4): each director and each trustee for debenture holders must give notice within 7 days of the receipt of the request: a deadline.
-- src:20471 | (4) Each director and each trustee for debenture holders must give
-- src:20472 | notice to the company of such matters relating to the director or the
-- src:20473 | trustee as may be necessary for the purposes of this section within
-- src:20474 | 7 days of the receipt of a request in writing for information as to such
-- src:20475 | matters.
@ref s 211(4) (src:20471-20475)
GIVEN who IS A Party
      `the number of days from the start of the trace to the last day for the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 210 act`
`s 211(4) a director or trustee for debenture holders must give notice within 7 days of the receipt of the request` MEANS
    PARTY who
    MUST `s 211(4) give notice to the company of the matters relating to the director or trustee`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the start of the trace to the last day for the notice`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY who BECAUSE "notice was not given to the company within 7 days of the receipt of the request in writing"

-- s 212(3): the company must lodge within 7 days of the making of the order: (a) a copy with the Registrar; (b) where the order relates to land, an office copy with the appropriate authority.
-- src:20552 | (3) Where an order is made under this section, every company in
-- src:20553 | relation to which the order is made must lodge within 7 days of the
-- src:20554 | making of the order —
-- src:20556 | (a) a copy of the order with the Registrar; and
-- src:20558 | (b) where the order relates to land, an office copy of the order
-- src:20559 | with the appropriate authority concerned with the
-- src:20560 | registration or recording of dealings in that land,
-- src:20562 | and every company which makes default in complying with this
-- src:20563 | section and every officer of the company who is in default shall be
-- src:20564 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:20565 | exceeding $2,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 212(3) (src:20552-20565)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days from the start of the trace to the last day for lodging` IS A NUMBER
      `the order relates to land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 210 act`
`s 212(3) the company must lodge within 7 days of the making of the order` MEANS
    IF `the order relates to land`
    THEN (PARTY Company `the name of the company`
          MUST `s 212(3)(a) lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar`
          WITHIN `the number of days from the start of the trace to the last day for lodging`
          HENCE FULFILLED
          LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "a copy of the order was not lodged with the Registrar within 7 days of the making of the order")
         RAND
         (PARTY Company `the name of the company`
          MUST `s 212(3)(b) lodge an office copy of the order with the appropriate authority`
          WITHIN `the number of days from the start of the trace to the last day for lodging`
          HENCE FULFILLED
          LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "an office copy of the order was not lodged with the appropriate authority within 7 days of the making of the order")
    ELSE PARTY Company `the name of the company`
         MUST `s 212(3)(a) lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar`
         WITHIN `the number of days from the start of the trace to the last day for lodging`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "a copy of the order was not lodged with the Registrar within 7 days of the making of the order"
